# For the planning group defined by its name, execute the given trajectory with that group.

# Execute the Cartesian trajectories for one planning group.

# Requests
# group_name: The planning group's name.
# sparse_trajectory: The (sparse) Cartesian trajectory for the group to execute.
#                    "Sparse" indicates that the trajectory may contain only a limited number of waypoints with their
#                    respective poses. The velocity and acceleration at these waypoints can be unspecified.
# dry_run: If set to true, the trajectory will be planned but not executed.
#          A dense trajectory will always be created in this case. The planner will make its best effort to populate
#          the velocity and acceleration properties for the dense trajectory. Default false.

# Response
# dense_trajectory: The dense trajectory is a trajectory prepared for execution by the real robot.
#                   Except for the first pose (0s), the duration of all waypoints is precisely 0.001 seconds,
#                   which corresponds to the Franka robot's control loop time.

std_msgs/Header header
string group_name
roport/CartesianTrajectory sparse_trajectory
bool dry_run
---
uint8 SUCCEEDED=0
uint8 FAILED=1
uint8 result_status
string result_msg
roport/CartesianTrajectory dense_trajectory
